# F alone, with Phi dropped. One row per part: the composed layer, the part it is composed from,
# and whether the part is local to the composing document.
#
# Incidence only, and the omission is the point
#   examples/diagramming/main.rs composes this and nothing wider, so the emitter is structurally
#   unable to read a magnitude. The incidence composes and the quantities do not, and a diagram
#   carries incidence. An emitter that could see a figure could render one, and a rendered figure
#   in a notation with no unit is the nonsense product entries/cross_layer_edges.sqlc already
#   names `the_product_nobody_should_use`.
#
# A type error, not a design decision
#   Reading the wider relation failed to compile: sqlx has no mapping for `pm.absence_reason` and
#   needs a feature for NUMERIC. The schema refused to hand a magnitude to a program with no use
#   for one, which is the DDL's typed absences paying out in a second language.
#
-- composition/parts.sqlc projected to F alone, with Phi dropped; one call activity per part.
SELECT p.composition, p.composed_layer, p.part_notation, p.part_filing, p.part_layer,
       (p.part_filing = p.composition) AS is_local
FROM (
    :compose(composition/parts.sqlc)
) p
